WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.089
This is a recording of the running app with fictional training records.

5
00:00:04.089 --> 00:00:06.223
Cloud responses and G P S are simulated.

9
00:00:06.223 --> 00:00:08.838
Sign in using your company username and password.

13
00:00:08.838 --> 00:00:10.225
Never share your password.

17
00:00:11.025 --> 00:00:16.402
First open the administrator invitation from N P I and choose your own username and password.

21
00:00:16.402 --> 00:00:20.507
After signing in, your company workspace shows only its permitted work.

25
00:00:20.507 --> 00:00:23.051
Ask N P I to correct missing contract sites.

29
00:00:23.851 --> 00:00:25.986
Open My team and choose Invite workers.

33
00:00:25.986 --> 00:00:29.379
Create the company link and share it privately with your team.

37
00:00:29.379 --> 00:00:33.648
The link expires after seven days and permits up to one hundred registrations.

41
00:00:33.648 --> 00:00:35.400
Workers enter their own details.

45
00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:38.718
New registrations appear under Pending workers.

49
00:00:38.718 --> 00:00:42.307
Verify each person belongs to your company, then approve or reject.

53
00:00:42.307 --> 00:00:46.003
Account approval grants access; it does not approve their work hours.

57
00:00:46.803 --> 00:00:49.026
Open Work orders and create an assignment.

61
00:00:49.026 --> 00:00:51.407
Choose a permitted contract site and service.

65
00:00:51.407 --> 00:00:53.471
Enter instructions, date and equipment.

69
00:00:53.471 --> 00:00:57.863
Select approved workers from your company and add a practical checklist, then save.

73
00:00:58.663 --> 00:01:00.786
Select all workers assigned to a crew job.

77
00:01:00.786 --> 00:01:06.446
Workers can capture attendance for the assigned crew, but each person keeps their own recorded and claimed time.

81
00:01:06.446 --> 00:01:09.832
Hauling assignments additionally record whole loads and a timecard.

85
00:01:10.632 --> 00:01:15.366
Use the overview and work orders to see activity and work waiting for company review.

89
00:01:15.366 --> 00:01:16.925
Refresh for updated records.

93
00:01:16.925 --> 00:01:22.661
An assignment reference photo identifies the site; workers must upload actual work evidence separately.

97
00:01:23.461 --> 00:01:24.586
Open submitted work.

101
00:01:24.586 --> 00:01:27.175
Compare recorded hours with each worker claim.

105
00:01:27.175 --> 00:01:31.451
Inspect both G P S events, accuracy, tasks and uploaded photos or timecards.

109
00:01:31.451 --> 00:01:35.221
Click a coordinate link to inspect that captured position on a map.

113
00:01:36.021 --> 00:01:40.370
If the record is correct, choose Approve and forward to N P I, then confirm.

117
00:01:40.370 --> 00:01:42.659
Your review is the first approval stage.

121
00:01:42.659 --> 00:01:46.837
N P I performs the final verification of the original evidence and hours.

125
00:01:47.637 --> 00:01:52.382
If work or hours need clarification, use Request correction and enter a specific reason.

129
00:01:52.382 --> 00:01:55.617
The worker corrects the claim or evidence and submits again.

133
00:01:55.617 --> 00:01:58.959
Never rewrite original G P S attendance to make a claim match.

137
00:01:59.759 --> 00:02:03.904
In My team you can reset a worker password, pause access or restore access.

141
00:02:03.904 --> 00:02:07.109
Disable unused invitation links to stop new registrations.

145
00:02:07.109 --> 00:02:09.209
Share replacement passwords privately.

149
00:02:09.209 --> 00:02:11.971
Existing work records remain available for review.

153
00:02:12.771 --> 00:02:16.658
Settings shows your company identity, timezone and available services.

157
00:02:16.658 --> 00:02:19.322
Ask N P I for additional sites or service types.

161
00:02:19.322 --> 00:02:23.431
Finish by checking work waiting for review and sign out on shared devices.

165
00:02:23.431 --> 00:02:25.818
Invoices will be added in a future release.
